==English==

===Etymology===
(weatherproofing) From original '''flashing material''' of [[copper]] or [[aluminum]] that [[reflect]]s flashes of [[sunlight]].

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-us-flashing.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*{{rhymes|æʃɪŋ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#  The '''[[weatherproofing|weatherproofed]] shielding''' put around objects which [[protrude]] from the [[roof]] of a [[building]], such as [[pipe]]s, [[chimney]]s, or the edges of other roofs to deflect [[water]] away from the [[seam]]s.
# The process of getting rid of gaps on shelves by bringing products from the back of the shelf to the front to create a 'fuller' shelf.
# The [[blink]]ing of a [[light]] source, such as a [[light bulb]] or [[computer]]'s [[cursor]].
#:''The incessant '''flashing''' of the neon sign kept the neighborhood awake.''
#An incidence of [[indecent exposure]].

===Verb===
'''flashing'''

# {{present participle of|[[flash]]}}  

